[3.006, "o", "\u001b[2A\u001b[?25h\r\r\n\r\r\n\r\r\n\u001b[1mð§ Available Tools:\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[2m─────────────────────\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[38;5;41m[1] current-time\u001b[m\r\r\n    \u001b[2;3mRetrieves precise current time with support for custom timezones, formats, and atomic clock sources (NTP). Useful for absolute time references.\u001b[m\r\r\n    \u001b[38;5;248mParameters: \u001b[mtimezone, format, locale, timeSource, ntpServer, ntpTimeoutMs\r\r\n\r\r\n\u001b[38;5;41m[2] timezone-tools\u001b[m\r\r\n    \u001b[2;3mConverts timestamps between timezones or Unix epochs (seconds/milliseconds), compares timezone offsets, or lists available zones. Supports ISO 8601 and custom formats.\u001b[m\r\r\n    \u001b[38;5;248mParameters: \u001b[moperation, targetTimezone, sourceTimezone, datetime, inputFormat, outputFormat, firstTimezone, secondTimezone, locale, search\r\r\n\r\r\n\u001b[38;5;41m[3] sleep\u001b[m\r\r\n    \u001b[2;3mBlocks execution for a specified duration in milliseconds. Essential for rate limiting, pacing sequences, or introducing controlled delays in workflows.\u001b[m\r\r\n    \u001b[38;5;248mParameters: \u001b[mmillisec"]
